{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And it shall be.</b> We know that HaShem knows whether they will believe or will not believe; only the verse speaks in response to Moses: if some of Israel do not believe the first sign, they will believe the last sign. And the verse says, 'to the sound of the sign,' but it has no sound; rather, the Torah speaks in the language of human beings, as in 'Death and life are in the hand of the tongue' (Proverbs 18:21). And the verse says 'the last sign,' even though there is a third sign there, because He did not show him now except these two signs, for the third he is destined to do."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:31:29.763949477Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}